  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th. The team has expanded to include Mike Chen and Lisa Ray. The project has reached a milestone with the completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th, and achieved a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two. The budget was initially $500,000 for Phase One, adjusted to $550,000, with a compliance plan budget of $55,000, and ultimately approved at $2M by the executive board. Partnership discussions with TechInnovate are underway, and a detailed report on Phase Two progress will be shared on November 20th."
